# Force LF everywhere. The reproducible-build bonus requires byte-identical
# output across machines; CRLF on Windows would change every file hash.
* text=auto eol=lf

# EXCEPT the HTTP fixtures. HTTP/1.1 framing IS carriage-return-line-feed: the
# blank line that ends the headers is \r\n\r\n, and a chunk length is followed
# by \r\n. Normalising these to LF silently breaks every HTTP test on a fresh
# clone while the working tree that committed them keeps passing.
test/fixtures/http-*.txt -text

*.png binary
*.der binary
